<body>
    <h1>Enterprise Data Naming Standards</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-1.Purpose"><strong>1. Purpo=
se</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  This page defines the <strong>enterprise-wide naming conventions</strong>=
 for all data modelling layers within the Allianz Data Platform (ADP).<br>
  It ensures consistent, readable, and platform=E2=80=91independent naming =
across:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"8=
fb5a3f6-f227-4230-a49f-2f0a7b5bc48a">Operational Data Store (ODS)</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"a=
76683b1-601e-4804-af6c-5e3be68539e8">Silver layer</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"0=
98f5e74-794f-432f-b480-ba414af71333">Gold layer</li>
</ul>
<p><br>
  All sub=E2=80=91pages inherit these core principles.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.GuidingPrinciples"><strong>2. Gui=
ding Principles</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  These principles apply to <strong>all layers</strong>, unless explicitly =
overridden in the layer-specific subpages.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.1Clarity"><strong>2.1 Clarity</st=
rong></h3>
<p><br>
  Names must be descriptive, unambiguous, and immediately understandable by=
 business and technical users.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.2Consistency"><strong>2.2 Consist=
ency</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Follow the same construction rules across all layers.<br>
  Each object name should follow a recognisable pattern.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.3Simplicity"><strong>2.3 Simplici=
ty</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Avoid unnecessary complexity, jargon, or processing metadata in names.</p=
>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.4Platform-neutral"><strong>2.4 Pl=
atform-neutral</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Naming must not encode physical implementation details such as datatype, =
DB technology, or source system encoding.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.5CaseConvention"><strong>2.5 Case=
 Convention</strong></h3>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"3=
809add6-39b3-4471-8ae4-ec367d3d1cea"><strong>ODS Layer</strong>: PascalCase=
 (inherits source system conventions)</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"9=
0098bf2-bc7c-4b04-b3e9-28ca27618ff4"><strong>Silver / Raw Vault / BDV</stro=
ng>:</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"6=
8c3265d-dabe-4c8b-a8a3-76a3f9ac714d"><strong>Gold Layer</strong>: PascalCas=
e (semantic model aligned to CFM)</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.6WordConstructionRules"><strong>2=
.6 Word Construction Rules</strong></h3>
<p><br><br></p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-3.NamingStructureforAttributes"><st=
rong>3. Naming Structure for Attributes</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  All business attributes follow this structure:</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-Subject+Qualifier(s)+Logicaldatatyp=
e"><strong>Subject+ Qualifier(s) + Logical data type</strong></h3>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Component</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Example</th>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Subject</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Main business entity</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Policy</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Qualifier(s)</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Additional context</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Renewal</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Logical data type</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Defines data category</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Date</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br><strong>Example Attribute Name:</strong><br><code>PolicyRenewalDate<=
/code></p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-4.ClassWords"><strong>4. Class Word=
s</strong></h2>
<p><br></p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-5.TableNamingStandards"><strong>5. =
Table Naming Standards</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-5.1ODSTables"><strong>5.1 ODS Table=
s</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Follow operational convention (usually PascalCase) =E2=80=94 see subpage.=
</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-5.2SilverLayer"><strong>5.2 Silver =
Layer</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Use <strong>SILVER_</strong> or domain-based prefixes.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-5.3RawVault/BusinessVault"><strong>=
5.3 Raw Vault / Business Vault</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Follow DV2.0 standards:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"1=
d356b30-2fa4-4007-b768-5ccac90bbce6"><code>HUB_&lt;entity&gt;</code></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"3=
ee4863d-0bdb-4612-b023-beeb64c1a3f5"><code>LNK_&lt;relationship&gt;</code><=
/li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"d=
27a291e-32a0-436d-ac22-8bf54fdbd4f8"><code>SAT_&lt;context&gt;</code></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"4=
c8690de-05e8-4d0a-a951-dd2a7b539642">HashKey and HashDiff conventions</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-5.4GoldLayer"><strong>5.4 Gold Laye=
r</strong></h3>
<p><br>
  Follow semantic consumption naming (see subpage):</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"7=
4a5261a-6815-47bf-9713-1c51420db54d"><code>F_&lt;BusinessProcess&gt;</code>=
</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"c=
a227922-610a-49e6-979f-888df01f8fd0"><code>D_&lt;BusinessConcept&gt;</code>=
</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"3=
ca68806-46d5-4e77-9683-97fe604a35e7"><code>V_&lt;SemanticView&gt;</code></l=
i>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-6.Abbreviations"><strong>6. Abbrevi=
ations</strong></h2>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"b=
5e34712-0b31-4533-b81b-2573429e27e2">Use full words unless length limits re=
quire abbreviation.</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"7=
6aad638-165c-4870-bb39-323f4dbf4b84">Acronyms UPPER CASE.</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"e=
9057436-050d-4558-918a-b4d577c6f495">All abbreviations must be taken from t=
he <strong>Master Abbreviation List</strong>.</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"8=
62dff2e-faa8-469f-a0ee-ab6ca4ce9f81">No creating new local abbreviations wi=
thout governance approval.</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-DataAttributeNamingConvention">Data=
 Attribute Naming Convention</h1>
<p>The goal of this naming convention is to ensure clarity, consistency, an=
d alignment with data principles across all data attributes</p>
<h2 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-GuidingPrinciples">Guiding Principl=
es</h2>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"87c2c863-bc9a-47c0-a107-034efc670a00">Clarity: Names shou=
ld be self-explanatory, readily understood by both technical and non-techni=
cal personnel.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"89bc3bac-9373-4a4a-9d5b-9100fc223cb3">Consistency: Adhere=
 to a uniform pattern across all data elements.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1ee37f97-4093-4a03-9255-c366553c4cec">Case Sensitivity: A=
dhere to a consistent case convention - PascalCase</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1e02afe4-28af-4a0a-9703-c7e8542586c0">Specificity: Naming=
 must be specific to the data point and incorporate details regarding the p=
urpose or context of the data element.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"012d9af7-022e-45d9-8f5c-32e35be98086">Brevity: Strive for=
 concise names while preserving clarity.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"669118a8-99b1-4807-81ef-14ccb6033dc9">Context: Acknowledg=
e the interconnected nature of our systems when naming data elements to ens=
ure seamless integration and avert conflicts.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3f0cc3d2-ef46-42cc-8924-2d75b976020e">Data Category Inclu=
sion: To be included in the data catalogue ONLY.</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 1494.36px;=
">
  <colgroup class=3D"">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 381.27px;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 391.543px;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 270.645px;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 420.371px;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 29.2773px;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <h6 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-1.PascalCase:">1. PascalCase:<=
/h6>
     <p>Variable name must be in PascalCase (i.e., the first letter of ever=
y word should be capitalized).</p></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-success conf-m=
acro output-inline" style=3D"text-decoration: none;color:#000000;" data-has=
body=3D"false" data-macro-name=3D"status">GREEN</span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <h6 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-2.Variablename:"><span style=
=3D"color:#172B4D;">2. Variable name:</span></h6>
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">This describes the data. It should b=
e self-explanatory, readily understood by both technical and non-technical =
personnel.&nbsp;</span></p></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-success conf-m=
acro output-inline" style=3D"text-decoration: none;color:#000000;" data-has=
body=3D"false" data-macro-name=3D"status">GREEN</span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <p>The strategic direction that DA team wants to proceed in is the cre=
ation, usage and<span>&nbsp;</span>alignment<span>&nbsp;</span>to an attrib=
uted CFM model(including derived fields).&nbsp;</p>
     <p>If a new attribute is required, best practice is to follow the form=
at SubjectQualifierDatatype.</p>
     <p>eg. PolicyInceptionDate</p>
     <ol>
      <li data-uuid=3D"dc8fc35e-6e3a-4e54-9b9d-bb273b38bce3">
       <p><strong>Subject</strong>: This is the main entity that the data a=
ttribute is about. It typically represents the primary object or entity in =
the context of the business domain. "Policy" is the subject because the att=
ribute pertains to a policy.</p></li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"c052d045-be3b-4d35-98b8-746012ab109a">
       <p><strong>Qualifier</strong>: This provides additional context or s=
pecificity to the subject.&nbsp; "Inception" is the qualifier because it sp=
ecifies that the date is related to the inception (start) of the policy.</p=
></li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"00c753fd-eef5-4b1d-9514-a0761c4db1f3">
       <p><strong>Logical DataType</strong>: This denotes the type of data =
the attribute holds, such as Date, Number, Text, etc.&nbsp; "Date" is impli=
citly understood as the data type.<span>&nbsp;</span><u><strong>Please note=
, physical datatype (eg Varchar, Integer, Bit etc.) should not be considere=
d while naming the attributes.</strong></u></p></li>
     </ol>
     <p><span>Please refer to the&nbsp;</span><strong>Master Abbreviations*=
*</strong><span>&nbsp;list mentioned at the bottom of this page</span></p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p><strong>Including the logical data type as a suffix with an undersc=
ore delimiter(e.g., _PCT, _NMBR) is acceptable when it improves readability=
 and prevents ambiguity, especially in cases where the attribute name alone=
 does not make the data type obvious.</strong></p></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <h6 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-3.IntegrationSpecificattribut=
es[INSTANDASpecific]"><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">3. Integration Specifi=
c attributes [INSTANDA Specific]</span></h6>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">Format:<strong>[Direction*]_[System=
/Microservice**]_[Description]</strong></span></p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">This is proposed by Product config =
team specifically for ALL integration attributes within the INSTANDA platfo=
rm. For each integration, existing attributes will be replicated/ new attri=
butes will be created&nbsp;</span></p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;"><strong>Direction</strong>: This de=
fines whether data is intended to be published (IN) to an integrated system=
 or (OUT) from an integrated system.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style=
=3D"color:#172B4D;">&nbsp;Section 1 of the Variable name must be created in=
 CAPITALS (i.e., "IN_" / "OUT_").</span></p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;"><strong>System/Microservice</strong=
>: Defines the target or source system that data is intended to be publishe=
d (IN) to an integrated system or (OUT) from an integrated system.</span></=
p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;"><strong>Description</strong>: Descr=
ibes the data attribute.</span></p>
      <p><br></p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">This is applicable to attributes th=
at fall in categories-&nbsp; 5.a, 5a.i and 5.b.&nbsp;</span><span>&nbsp;</s=
pan><span>Any attributes needed for the data platform, product config team =
proposed to create an additional attribute without the IN_/OUT_ prefix.</sp=
an></p>
      <p><br></p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><br></p>
      <p>In INSTANDA, product configurators are required to configure integ=
ration-specific attributes and maintain distinct&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-=
link" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/azure/logic-apps/logic-apps=
-enterprise-integration-liquid-transform?tabs=3Dconsumption&amp;source=3Ddo=
cs" rel=3D"nofollow" style=3D"">liquid template</a>s for each integration. =
The direction prefix aids in tracking attribute dependencies, while the sys=
tem/microservice component provides context for which integration the attri=
bute is utilized.</p>
      <p>Since interfaces are designed based on the specifications of the t=
arget system (interface contracts) that are still evolving, there have been=
 instances where changes in the interface contract have necessitated the re=
configuration of attributes (such as EPC requirements and Contract/Booking =
payload).</p>
      <p><strong>Implications:<span>&nbsp;</span></strong><span>Attributes =
must be duplicated, resulting in data redundancy within INSTANDA. However, =
as this does not affect INSTANDA's performance, the Product Config team pre=
fers this method.</span></p>
      <p><span>It ensures the stability of liquid templates, and if any int=
erface contract changes occur over time, only the relevant attributes need =
modification, avoiding a comprehensive impact analysis and extensive produc=
t configuration changes.</span></p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#09326C;">This advantage does not extend to c=
onstants within a package, which remain unchanged across integrations. Ther=
efore, it has been decided that constants can be exempted from adhering to =
this naming convention.</span></p>
      <p><span style=3D"color:#09326C;">Integration attributes classified a=
s constants should be tagged in the Data Dictionary to ensure a consistent =
approach is applied across all packages.</span></p>
      <p><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td class=3D"highlight-#fff0b3 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=3D"#=
fff0b3" style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper" title=3D"">
      <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-moved conf-mac=
ro output-inline" style=3D"text-decoration: none;color:#172B4D;" data-hasbo=
dy=3D"false" data-macro-name=3D"status">YELLOW</span></p>
      <p>Attribute names should convey only the inherent meaning of the dat=
a, not information related to processing or usage. To ensure consistency ac=
ross the ecosystem and stability as data pathways evolve,<strong><span>&nbs=
p;</span>it is advisable to avoid including directional information (such a=
s IN and OUT) in attribute names. Including such information can lead to in=
consistency and confusion, especially if the direction of data flow changes=
, such as when data mastership is altered.</strong></p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <ol>
      <li data-uuid=3D"e6cec59f-7126-4f00-8e5f-63673ccbcd29"><span style=3D=
"color:#172B4D;">"<span>System/Microservice" name needs to be standardized&=
nbsp; values captured in RDM repository</span></span></li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"2d401739-e0c5-420c-838a-0cb69c88a7a6"><span style=3D=
"color:#172B4D;">For the ODS creation, avoid data redundancy by reusing exi=
sting attributes from CFM whenever possible.</span></li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"ed360163-869b-45f3-aa70-d1079e372053">IN_/&nbsp;OUT_=
 pref<span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">ix</span><span>&nbsp;</span>w<span styl=
e=3D"color:#172B4D;">ould be removed while creating the views. eg. IN_Radar=
_QuoteSubId would become Radar_QuoteSubId.</span></li>
     </ol></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <h6 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-4.ProductCode:"><span style=3D=
"color:#172B4D;">4. Product Code:</span></h6>
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">When the variable name defines data =
that is unique to a single defined product and requires a Product ID, the P=
roduct Code can be used, i.e., "_BX" at the end of the variable name. Note:=
 This applies to variables that have been confirmed as unique only, and onl=
y used as an exception.</span></p></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-success conf-m=
acro output-inline" style=3D"text-decoration: none;color:#000000;" data-has=
body=3D"false" data-macro-name=3D"status">GREEN</span>&nbsp;</p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">Since it is difficult to assess the reusability(eg. for Clauses)., it w=
as agreed that this would be done on exception basis in alignment with DA t=
eam.</td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <h6 id=3D"EnterpriseDataNamingStandards-5.DataType">5. Data Type</h6>
     <p>Where data is only used within Instanda and regardless of whether t=
he variable comes from a Question or a Calculation, the output format (data=
 type) is what we are interested in because it affects how we can use the v=
ariable within other variables. For example, it helps prevent the user from=
 trying to carry out an impossible calculation such as trying to multiply a=
 number with a date.</p>
     <p><br></p>
     <p><span style=3D"color:#172B4D;">&nbsp;</span></p></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-success conf-m=
acro output-inline" style=3D"text-decoration: none;color:#000000;" data-has=
body=3D"false" data-macro-name=3D"status">GREEN</span></p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td">
     <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
      <p class=3D"title conf-macro-render">Recommedation:</p>
      <p>The list of abbreviations need to be mastered in a repository for =
re-use.</p>
      <p>Data modelling best practice is to include data types as a<span>&n=
bsp;</span><em>suffix</em>, not a prefix e.g "Loss Notification<span>&nbsp;=
</span><strong>Date</strong>".</p>
     </div></td>
    <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"confluence=
Td"><br></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>**Master Abbreviations<br><br></strong>(<em>Please note, the fol=
lowing list has been discussed in Instanda COE - data attribute governance =
forum on<span>&nbsp;</span></em><span><time datetime=3D"2025-11-13" class=
=3D"date-past">13 Nov 2025</time></span><em><span>&nbsp;</span>and is good =
to start. This list can evolve further based on suggestions for improvement=
s. Also, alignment to the list while configuring the attributes on Instanda=
 will be a fix forward approach and this wont impact the existing attribute=
s/variables already configured.</em></p>
